{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"N23\",\"lines\":\"rr-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N23.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَتَوَاصَوْا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"وَعَمِلُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The pasture that abundantly fits the herd is provision put to use. Heard beside عَمِلُوا as purposeful use, the verse pictures action drawing on a sustaining ground.\",\"reason\":\"The rare وصى لها المرتع يصي وصيا names pasture that meets livestock abundantly; عَمِلُوا includes إعمال الشيء واستعماله. The senses meet as fitting resource and its deliberate use.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N23.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَتَوَاصَوْا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ\",\"after\":\"The pasture sense is abundance of what suits the herd, and الصَّالِحَات can carry suitability as well as goodness. Heard together, righteous deeds look like acts fitted to nourish and repair the community.\",\"reason\":\"The rare وصى لها المرتع يصي وصيا means pasture abundantly suited to livestock; الصَّالِحَات names what is good and proper, with الصلاح للشيء ملاءمته. Both meet in fitness for what needs sustaining.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N24\",\"lines\":\"rrr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N24.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"بِٱلصَّبْرِ\",\"target_ar\":\"ءَامَنُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The rare صبر sense evokes an oath imposed by force or a person held for death, while ءَامَنُوا۟ names assent that settles in the heart. Faith sounds as inward trust against compelled profession, marking the believers’ escape from coercion.\",\"reason\":\"The dictionary gives الصبر الإكراه and صبرت يمينه أي حلفته; the target’s تصديق يطمئن إليه القلب is settled belief. Forced oath and trusting assent pull in opposite directions.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N24.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"بِٱلصَّبْرِ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَعَمِلُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The group is described through deliberate deeds, while the rare صبر image pins someone in place under compulsion. The pairing makes righteous action an exercise of agency set against coercive detention and imposed death.\",\"reason\":\"The rare Arabic sense is حبس القهر للقتل أو اليمين; عَمِلُوا means deliberate doing or putting something to use. Compelled confinement restrains the agency that purposeful action exercises.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N24.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"بِٱلصَّبْرِ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَتَوَاصَوْا۟\",\"after\":\"The rare sense binds someone through a forced oath, while تَوَاصَوْا describes people mutually passing counsel and charge. The verse’s shared counsel can be heard as a communal bond set against an imposed one.\",\"reason\":\"The dictionary gives صبرت يمينه أي حلفته and قتل صبر; the target includes عهد موصول إلى غيره and تبادل الوصية بين القوم. Compulsion gives way to reciprocal counsel.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N25\",\"lines\":\"--r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N25.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"بِٱلصَّبْرِ\",\"target_ar\":\"بِٱلْحَقِّ\",\"after\":\"The hard stone gives truth a tangible image of firmness. The pair makes the counsel of al-ḥaqq sound like a claim that can bear weight and hold its ground.\",\"reason\":\"The rare الصبرة من الحجارة ما اشتد وغلظ names hard, coarse stone; al-ḥaqq carries ثبات مطابق للواقع and إحكام رصين. Both senses meet in firmness.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N26\",\"lines\":\"nrn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N26.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"بِٱلصَّبْرِ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَعَمِلُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Deliberate doing meets an affair with no way out as action within a crisis. This is a thin scene of agency under pressure.\",\"reason\":\"The rare أم صبور is an أمر لا منفذ له عنه; عَمِلُوا names purposeful action. The senses complement one another as predicament and action within it.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N26.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"بِٱلصَّبْرِ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَتَوَاصَوْا۟\",\"after\":\"The rare صبور crisis gives the mutual counsel a scene: a community in a great affair with no escape addresses one another from within it. Counsel and patience then sound like shared support for facing what cannot simply be left.\",\"reason\":\"The Arabic أم صبور means أمر شديد لا منفذ له عنه; تَوَاصَوْا means تبادل الوصية بين القوم. The counsel is pictured as passed among people caught in the same severe affair.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N26.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"بِٱلصَّبْرِ\",\"target_ar\":\"بِٱلْحَقِّ\",\"after\":\"The clause can hear al-ḥaqq as the settled reality of a crisis that offers no exit. This is a thin link: truth names what is factually established, not necessarily what is painful.\",\"reason\":\"The rare أم صبور is an أمر لا منفذ له عنه, while al-ḥaqq is ثبات مطابق للواقع. The pair can picture an unavoidable affair as a hard reality.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N27\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N28\",\"lines\":\"nrr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N28.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"بِٱلصَّبْرِ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَعَمِلُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The rare ṣibr is a bitter remedy, while عَمِلُوا can mean deliberate use. Together they make action the application of medicine.\",\"reason\":\"The dictionary glosses الصبر بكسر الباء as عصارة شجرة and as bitter medicine; عَمِلُوا includes إعمال الشيء واستعماله. The remedy and its purposeful use complement one another.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N28.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"بِٱلصَّبْرِ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ\",\"after\":\"The rare ṣibr sense is a bitter remedy; الصَّالِحَات are acts of repair and good order. Together they cast righteous deeds as medicine whose taste may be harsh while its work restores.\",\"reason\":\"The sources call الصبر بكسر الباء this الدواء المر; the target names الصلاح ضد الفساد and الصلح إزالة النفار بين الناس. Bitter medicine and restorative deeds meet in the image of a cure.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N28.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"بِٱلصَّبْرِ\",\"target_ar\":\"بِٱلْحَقِّ\",\"after\":\"The rare ṣibr is a bitter medicine, and al-ḥaqq is truth to which the group gives counsel. Heard together, truth becomes a bitter but healing remedy that the community urges one another to take.\",\"reason\":\"The dictionary gives الصبر هذا الدواء المر; the target بِٱلْحَقِّ names ثبات مطابق للواقع. The senses form the image of factual truth as medicine with a bitter taste.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N29\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N30\",\"lines\":\"-n-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N30.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"بِٱلصَّبْرِ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَتَوَاصَوْا۟\",\"after\":\"White clouds stacked over dense ones suggest one layer resting on another; mutual counsel likewise accumulates across the group. The comparison is thin because تَوَاصَوْا names exchanged counsel rather than physical support.\",\"reason\":\"The rare الصبير is سحاب أبيض يصبر بعضه فوق بعض; the target includes وصل الشيء بالشيء and تبادل الوصية بين القوم. The senses can picture counsel as a layer of support laid upon another.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N31\",\"lines\":\"rnr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N31.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"بِٱلصَّبْرِ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ\",\"after\":\"A pile of food offers an image of provision gathered together; الصَّالِحَات names good deeds that repair and benefit. The pair lets the community’s righteous deeds appear as a store of nourishment shared among them.\",\"reason\":\"The rare الصبرة من الطعام بعضه فوق بعض is food piled together; the target carries goodness and restoration. The two senses make an image of accumulated deeds as communal provision.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N31.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"بِٱلصَّبْرِ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَتَوَاصَوْا۟\",\"after\":\"The broad mat and piled food form a setting where people can gather; تَوَاصَوْا supplies the mutual exchange around it. The link is generic because the food sense does not itself mean counsel.\",\"reason\":\"The rare صبير الخوان is a broad sheet spread beneath food; the target means تبادل الوصية بين القوم. A shared eating place can frame the mutual counsel.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N31.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"بِٱلصَّبْرِ\",\"target_ar\":\"بِٱلْحَقِّ\",\"after\":\"A purchase as صبرة leaves a food heap unweighed and unmeasured, while al-ḥaqq can name the due that belongs to its owner. Heard together, counsel of right gives a measure of justice to what is handled as bulk.\",\"reason\":\"The rare phrase اشتريت الشيء صبرة means buying it بلا وزن ولا كيل; al-ḥaqq includes حق مخصوص يملكه صاحبه. The unmeasured heap contrasts with a bounded entitlement.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N32\",\"lines\":\"-n-r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N32.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"بِٱلصَّبْرِ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَعَمِلُوا۟\",\"after\":\"A reprisal under قصاص is a concrete deliberate act, so it touches the broad doing named by عَمِلُوا. The overlap stays at the level of action; the verse’s object الصَّالِحَات still specifies good deeds.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense is فليقتص, killing in retribution; عَمِلُوا names الفعل المقصود والعمل. One is a specific act and the other is broad purposeful doing.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N32.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"بِٱلصَّبْرِ\",\"target_ar\":\"بِٱلْحَقِّ\",\"after\":\"The rare صبر sense denotes legal retaliation for homicide, while al-ḥaqq can name what is due to its owner. The pair makes al-ḥaqq a claim administered in proportion, not merely an abstract truth.\",\"reason\":\"The sources gloss أَصْبَرَهُ as قتله بقود; al-ḥaqq includes حق مخصوص يملكه صاحبه. Retaliation and the rightful claim meet as due justice.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N33\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N34\",\"lines\":\"--n\"}\n{\"id\":\"N34.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"بِٱلصَّبْرِ\",\"target_ar\":\"بِٱلْحَقِّ\",\"after\":\"A mountain’s central mass gives an image of what is firmly established; al-ḥaqq likewise names settled reality. The comparison is broad because the target does not itself mean mountain or height.\",\"reason\":\"The rare الصبير is الجبل ووسطه; al-ḥaqq carries ثبات مطابق للواقع. The mountain’s solidity can picture truth’s firmness, though the link remains general.\"}"}}
